---
import { loadManifest } from '../lib/manifest.mjs';
import '../styles/global.css';
const manifest = loadManifest();
const tableCount = Object.keys(manifest.tables).length;
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow" />
    <meta name="description" content="Critical Minerals Atlas development scaffold. Source data has not yet been loaded." />
    <title>Critical Minerals Atlas · Development scaffold</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
    <header class="masthead">
      <a class="wordmark" href="/" aria-label="Critical Minerals Atlas home">
        <svg width="28" height="28" viewBox="0 0 28 28" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m14 1 12 7v12l-12 7L2 20V8Z" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"/><path d="m2 8 12 7 12-7M14 15v12M14 1v14" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"/></svg>
        <span>Critical Minerals <strong>Atlas</strong></span>
      </a>
      <span class="environment">Development scaffold</span>
    </header>
    <main id="main" tabindex="-1">
      <div class="release-strip" aria-label="Build metadata">
        <p><span>Data as of</span> <strong>Not yet available</strong></p>
        <p><span>Build release</span> <strong>{manifest.release_tag}</strong></p>
      </div>
      <section class="intro" aria-labelledby="page-title">
        <p class="eyebrow">Phase 0 · Repository foundation</p>
        <h1 id="page-title">A sourced view of the<br class="desktop-break" /> world's critical minerals.</h1>
        <p class="lede">Where deposits are, how mature they are, and who operates them. Starting with rare earth elements, nickel and cobalt.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="empty-state" aria-labelledby="empty-title">
        <div class="survey-mark" aria-hidden="true"><span></span></div>
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Data status</p>
          <h2 id="empty-title">No records loaded</h2>
          <p>This build verifies the repository and empty data pipeline. No sources have been ingested, and no deposit locations or mineral statistics are available yet.</p>
          <p class="next-step">Next: register sources and verify download manifests.</p>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section class="foundation" aria-labelledby="foundation-title">
        <div class="section-heading"><h2 id="foundation-title">Built for traceable evidence</h2><span>Implementation principles</span></div>
        <div class="principles">
          <article><span class="index">01</span><h3>Every value has a source</h3><p>Published facts will carry a source URL, retrieval date and evidence grade.</p></article>
          <article><span class="index">02</span><h3>Maturity stays visible</h3><p>Occurrences, estimates, resources, reserves and operating sites will remain distinguishable.</p></article>
          <article><span class="index">03</span><h3>Data stays portable</h3><p>The completed Atlas will pair every map view with a table, downloadable data and print exports.</p></article>
        </div>
      </section>
      <details class="build-details">
        <summary>Build details</summary>
        <dl><div><dt>Pipeline status</dt><dd>Empty scaffold</dd></div><div><dt>Canonical table structures</dt><dd>{tableCount}</dd></div><div><dt>Loaded records</dt><dd>0</dd></div><div><dt>Sources in this build</dt><dd>0</dd></div></dl>
        <p>These are build diagnostics, not measures of mineral coverage. Data ingestion and the interactive map are later implementation steps.</p>
      </details>
    </main>
    <footer><p>Critical Minerals Atlas</p><p>Local development · No data release</p></footer>
  </body>
</html>
